cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or discuss this concept, please cite this repository."
title: "Self-Calibrating Spatial Reaction-Mass Actuation Platform"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Dik"
    given-names: "Philip"
date-released: 2026-09-17
version: "0.4-en"
abstract: >-
  A generalized self-calibrating reaction-mass actuation architecture using
  controlled internal masses and spatial guideways to generate programmable
  force, torque, vibration, attitude response, and surface-coupled locomotion.
  A preferred embodiment uses a magnetic or ferromagnetic mover in a closed
  electromagnetic guide with phase-selective actuation and a learned
  force/torque response map.
keywords:
  - reaction-mass actuator
  - spatial reaction-mass actuation
  - distributed electromagnetic actuation
  - closed-loop guideway
  - phase-selective actuation
  - system identification
  - force torque response map
  - inertial locomotion
  - active balancing
  - impulse assistance
  - spherical mobile robot
  - hopping robot
